{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563923-v20-ish-preferred-combat-health-system-s","id":1563923,"title":"[V20-ish] Preferred Combat / Health System(s)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-09-08T14:53:42-07:00","id":1563923,"title":"[V20-ish] Preferred Combat / Health System(s)","content":"Upon re-reading VtM 20th rulebook, I realized that I've been technically running combat and health wrong. V20 apparently has no rules relating to the idea of damage &quot;wrapping around,&quot; (full track of bashing transforms into lethal, lethal to agg.), and I had mistakenly thought final death only occurred when the health track completely filled up with aggravated. However, further reading of other 20th anniversary editions, as well as some reading online, revealed that V20 DA and other 20th editions has the upgrading damage rules, while V5 is the only VtM system (to my knowledge) that has the ruling that Final Death occurs after an entire track of agg. damage.<br /> <br /> My question, for those more experienced ST'ing than me, is what is your preferred manner of handling combat, specifically with what causes Final Death, (one agg after torpor, or full health track of agg), and also about how initiative is handled (declare actions reversed order, or just perform actions in order of highest initiative)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28584-matter911","name":"Matter911","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-08T22:19:11-07:00","id":1563929,"title":"","content":"You're mixing signals here.<br /> <br /> One way to look at it is Aggravated Damage is different from Upgrading Damage: A punch will cause Bashing. Punching someone with a full Lethal track will upgrade the damage to Agg, but the damage <i>dealt</i> is still Bashing.<br /> <br /> Vampire distinguishes from other RPGs, including within WoD, that Final Death is not a consequence of losing HP. Instead it requires a specific cause.<br /> <br /> Damage causes torpor (and penalties) and the need for healing. Final Death requires either:<br /> <br /> 1. Damage <i><u><b>from a Bane</b></u></i> on a Torpid Vampire. That's the best wording the books don't always get right, the damage must come from a source that causes Aggravated by itself.<br /> <br /> 2. Complete body destruction, which is not to be measured by Health Levels. It is deliberately a descriptive thing. Continuously punching the torpid vampire won't kill it.<br /> <br /> Another point and one that will help you across games, is that death is not about combat balance, this is the bigger misconception here. Combat is about a character suffering mechanic effects from damage and eventually being rendered unable to participate.<br /> <br /> Once a character can't participate in combat, it is fluff. If the character lives or dies is just about what kind of stories you want to play.<br /> <br /> In Vampire, dying as a result of a combat action is rare and not necessarily a good game element. A torpid vampire is already out of commission, you can execute later if you wish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-09T23:31:36-07:00","id":1563950,"title":"","content":"Finding out you got some understanding wrong about part of rule x in edition y is classic storyteller. Only recently I realized burning blood on Potence in V20 grants automatic successes per <i>turn </i>not <i>action. </i>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> As for combat I rip out most of the maneuvers and the initiate system the latter which I believe most everyone does.<br /> <br /> For agg I'd run when you take a full health track+1 of aggravated but usually I avoid spamming non capped sources of aggravated, or at least play very careful with them. Don't really want a strong gangrel to roll nine successes and deal 14 dice or something of agg.<br /> <br /> It's a wish of mine to see a let's play with the original designers of the initiative system actually run through a game using it because I want to see it work as intended I still can't picture it.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-18T04:32:20-07:00","id":1564165,"title":"","content":"I basically reserve it for ST fiat. Usually, you need to be decapitated, put in a woodchipper, or left in the sunlight (or fire).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}